  <p class="section-label">Using the app</p>
  <ul class="feature-list">
    <li><strong>Categories and targets</strong> Group spending, set a monthly or save-by date target, and see what is still available.</li>
    <li><strong>Credit cards</strong> Spending on a card sets aside the payment in its own category.</li>
    <li><strong>Reports</strong> Spending by category and a net-worth history, on the device that holds the data.</li>
    <li><strong>More than one currency</strong> Foreign accounts convert with public exchange rates. The budget’s home currency stays put.</li>
    <li><strong>Share a budget</strong> Invite someone through iCloud. They see that budget, and we are not in the middle.</li>
    <li><strong>Receipts</strong> Attach a photo or scan a receipt on device. The image stays with the transaction.</li>
    <li><strong>Backups</strong> Export an archive you can restore later, plus a daily copy in your iCloud Drive.</li>
    <li><strong>Bring a plan with you</strong> A guided import reads a CSV export of a register and a category plan.</li>
    <li><strong>Expense tracking</strong> Spending is recorded against categories.</li>
    <li><strong>Registered accounts</strong> RRSP, TFSA, and RESP track contribution room, including a spousal RRSP. An RRSP withdrawal can show an estimated withholding tax. That figure is not tax advice.</li>
  </ul>
